(Evidence Brief - Warming Continues) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Evidence Brief: Global Warming Is Continuing) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Purpose) Tj
T*
(This classroom evidence brief summarizes several independent lines of observation that) Tj
T*
(support the proposition that global warming is continuing. It is a compact teaching) Tj
T*
(document, not a replacement for the original scientific assessments listed below.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Long-term surface temperature) Tj
T*
(Global mean surface temperature is evaluated over decades because individual years are) Tj
T*
(affected by El Nino, La Nina, volcanic aerosols, and weather variability. Multiple) Tj
T*
(independent temperature products use different combinations of land stations, ships, and) Tj
T*
(ocean buoys. Despite methodological differences, they show a persistent long-term) Tj
T*
(warming trend relative to nineteenth-century conditions. A cool month, cold winter, or) Tj
T*
(short plateau does not cancel a multi-decade global trend.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Ocean heat content) Tj
T*
(The ocean absorbs most of the excess heat retained by the climate system. Measurements) Tj
T*
(from ships, moorings, satellites, and profiling floats show increasing ocean heat) Tj
T*
(content over long periods. Ocean heat is important evidence because it integrates) Tj
T*
(changes over time and is less dominated by short-lived atmospheric fluctuations.) Tj
T*
(Continued heat accumulation is consistent with an ongoing planetary energy imbalance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Cryosphere observations) Tj
T*
(Glaciers in many regions have lost mass, the Greenland and Antarctic ice sheets have) Tj
T*
(experienced net mass loss, and Arctic sea ice has declined over the satellite era. No) Tj
T*
(single glacier proves a global trend, because local snowfall and circulation matter. The) Tj
T*
(value of the evidence comes from coherent changes across many regions and several) Tj
T*
(independent observing systems.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Sea level and physical consistency) Tj
T*
(Global mean sea level rises when ocean water expands as it warms and when land ice) Tj
T*
(melts. Tide gauges and satellite altimetry provide complementary records. Rising ocean) Tj
T*
(heat, shrinking land ice, and rising sea level are physically connected indicators.) Tj
T*
(Agreement among these indicators makes the inference stronger than reliance on surface) Tj
T*
(temperature alone.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Attribution and uncertainty) Tj
T*
(Climate models and observations are compared with natural factors such as solar) Tj
T*
(variability and volcanic activity, and with human influences such as greenhouse gases) Tj
T*
(and aerosols. Uncertainty remains in the magnitude of some regional effects and in) Tj
T*
(short-term timing. Uncertainty does not mean that every explanation is equally likely.) Tj
T*
(The broad warming signal and the dominant contribution of human greenhouse gas emissions) Tj
T*
(are supported by multiple evidence streams.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(How to use this brief in debate) Tj
T*
